  "tagline": "Vercel's agent stack as cloud primitives: gateway, sandbox, workflows, connect.",
  "description": "Vercel's Agent Stack post (2026-06-20) names the AI SDK and the eve framework for the agent loop, AI Gateway (\"the CDN for tokens\") across model providers, Vercel Sandbox microVMs for agent-written code, Workflow SDK for durable runs, Vercel Connect for short-lived scoped credentials and Chat SDK for chat platforms. Other Vercel pages add pieces mapped here: Drives for persistent Sandbox storage (vercel.com/ai), Queues (Vercel docs) and Fluid compute for long IO-bound work (Guillermo Rauch's 2025 AI Cloud post). eve's docs add first-class channels for Slack, Teams, Discord, Telegram, Twilio and iMessage, with Chat SDK adapters optional for other services, and default tools that include bash, read_file and write_file but no separate edit tool; grep and glob are opt-in. The stack is model-agnostic; Vercel's reference doesn't prescribe a model.",
